-- Cases for the encoding of the Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) 07-a0-00 and the Regulations in scope:
-- at least one case per encoded rule, taken from the words of the source, rule by rule. The cases for
-- consecutive agreements (the brief for this run) are in cases-consecutive.l4.
-- Where the fork register records two readings, the case asserts both, so that a change to the reading
-- taken cannot pass silently. Day counts follow the Interpretation Act 1984 ss 61-62.
-- Weekdays used: 1 Mar 2026 Sun; 1 May 2026 Fri; 26 Sep 2026 Sat; 3 Oct 2026 Sat; 5 Oct 2026 Mon;
-- 1 Dec 2026 Tue; 5 Dec 2026 Sat; 7 Dec 2026 Mon; 4 Jan 2027 Mon.
-- LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`
IMPORT `regulations-1989`
IMPORT `part-6-boundary`
IMPORT `part-3-div-3-retaliatory-action`
IMPORT `part-5-termination`
IMPORT `part-4-div-1-rent-and-bonds`
IMPORT `part-7-transitional-2024`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-extra`

§ `Fixtures`

`no holidays` MEANS EMPTY

`a periodic agreement P` MEANS `the periodic agreement` "P" `between` "L" `and` (LIST "T1", "T2") `for` "1 Example St" `from day` (`day number` 2025 3 1) `at weekly rent` 500

`a fixed term F for 2026` MEANS `a fixed term` "F" `between` "L" `and` (LIST "T1") `for` "1 Example St" `from day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `to day` (`day number` 2026 12 31) `at weekly rent` 500

`an empty history` MEANS `Rent history` WITH `agreements` IS EMPTY, `variations` IS EMPTY

-- A fixed-term agreement for 2026 with the given s 70A notices, delivery of possession and termination.
GIVEN ns  IS A LIST OF `Notice under s 70A`
      dl  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      te  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`the 2026 fixed term with notices` ns `, delivered up` dl `, terminated` te MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS "F"
        `lessor`                                         IS "L"
        `granted by`                                     IS "L"
        `tenants`                                        IS LIST "T1"
        `premises`                                       IS "1 Example St"
        `kind`                                           IS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
        `rent basis`                                     IS `a fixed amount`
        `entered into on`                                IS `day number` 2026 1 1
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS `day number` 2026 1 1
        `expiry day`                                     IS JUST (`day number` 2026 12 31)
        `weekly rent`                                    IS 500
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS FALSE
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS ns
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS dl
        `terminated on`                                  IS te
        `status`                                         IS `no special status`

GIVEN who IS A `Party`, g IS A NUMBER, pd IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice under s 70A`
`a s 70A notice by` who `given on day` g `for possession on day` pd MEANS
    `Notice under s 70A` WITH `given by` IS who, `given on` IS g, `possession day specified` IS pd

-- An agreement with the given status facts, otherwise the periodic agreement P.
GIVEN sf IS A `Status facts`
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`P with status` sf MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS "P"
        `lessor`                                         IS "L"
        `granted by`                                     IS "L"
        `tenants`                                        IS LIST "T1", "T2"
        `premises`                                       IS "1 Example St"
        `kind`                                           IS `a periodic tenancy`
        `rent basis`                                     IS `a fixed amount`
        `entered into on`                                IS `day number` 2025 3 1
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS `day number` 2025 3 1
        `expiry day`                                     IS NOTHING
        `weekly rent`                                    IS 500
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS FALSE
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS EMPTY
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS NOTHING
        `terminated on`                                  IS NOTHING
        `status`                                         IS sf

GIVEN which IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Status facts`
`the status with only limb set:` which MEANS
    `Status facts` WITH
        `the lessor is an employer in the Table to r 5B(2A) and a tenant is its employee`                       IS which EQUALS 1
        `the lessor is the Housing Authority or a GEHA department and the premises are let to a Government employee under the GEHA` IS which EQUALS 2
        `the lessor is the WA Country Health Service and a tenant is employed or engaged by it`                IS which EQUALS 3
        `the premises are Butler's Cottage, Government House`                                                  IS which EQUALS 4
        `the lessor is an agency in the Table to r 5B(3)`                                                      IS which EQUALS 5
        `the Crown is the lessor and a tenant is an officer of a department in the Table to r 5B(4)`           IS which EQUALS 6
        `the Housing Authority is the lessor`                                                                  IS which EQUALS 7
        `the Housing Authority is a party, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting` IS which EQUALS 8
        `the WA Country Health Service is the tenant, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting to its staff` IS which EQUALS 9
        `the premises are a residential unit in Foyer Oxford and the agreement is with Foundation Housing Limited` IS which EQUALS 10
        `the agreement is the renewal or extension of an agreement`                                            IS which EQUALS 11
        `the premises are south of the 26th parallel of south latitude`                                        IS which EQUALS 12
        `the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises`                                                IS which EQUALS 13
        `a court order under s 84 disapplies s 30(1) or s 31A to the agreement`                                IS which EQUALS 14

§ `Interpretation Act 1984 ss 61-62, through the day-number helpers (the library module's own examples)`

#ASSERT `day number` 2026 1 1 EQUALS 20454
-- s 62(2): "a month beginning on 15 January ends on 14 February and a month beginning on 30 or 31 January
-- ends on 28 February (or 29 February in a leap year)".
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 1 `months beginning on day` (`day number` 2026 1 15) EQUALS `day number` 2026 2 14
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 1 `months beginning on day` (`day number` 2026 1 30) EQUALS `day number` 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 1 `months beginning on day` (`day number` 2028 1 31) EQUALS `day number` 2028 2 29
-- s 62(3): "a period of 6 months beginning on 15 August ends on 14 February and a period of 6 months
-- beginning on 30 or 31 August ends on 28 February (or 29 February in a leap year)".
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 6 `months beginning on day` (`day number` 2026 8 15) EQUALS `day number` 2027 2 14
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 6 `months beginning on day` (`day number` 2027 8 31) EQUALS `day number` 2028 2 29
-- s 61(1)(b) with s 62: the 12 months after 1 March 2025 end on 1 March 2026; after 29 February 2024, on
-- 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 12 `months after day` (`day number` 2025 3 1) EQUALS `day number` 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 12 `months after day` (`day number` 2024 2 29) EQUALS `day number` 2025 2 28
-- s 61(1)(f): 60 clear days lie between 1 March and 1 May 2026; FK-06 both ways.
#ASSERT `the number of clear days between day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `and day` (`day number` 2026 5 1) EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the first day not less than` 60 `days after day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) EQUALS `day number` 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `FK-06 reading B -- the first day not less than` 60 `days after day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) EQUALS `day number` 2026 4 30
-- s 61(1)(g): from 1 May to 30 June 2026 is 60 days.
#ASSERT `the number of days from day` (`day number` 2026 5 1) `to day` (`day number` 2026 6 30) EQUALS 60
-- s 61(2): Saturday 3 October 2026 is an excluded day; Monday 5 October is not, unless it is a holiday.
#ASSERT `is day` (`day number` 2026 10 3) `an excluded day, given the holidays` `no holidays`
#ASSERT NOT (`is day` (`day number` 2026 10 5) `an excluded day, given the holidays` `no holidays`)
#ASSERT `is day` (`day number` 2026 10 5) `an excluded day, given the holidays` (LIST (`day number` 2026 10 5))
-- s 61(1)(b), (e): 7 days after Saturday 26 September 2026 ends on Saturday 3 October; the thing may be
-- done on Monday 5 October.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after day` (`day number` 2026 9 26) `, given the holidays` `no holidays` EQUALS `day number` 2026 10 5

