#ASSERT `r 5CB -- s 31(1B)(b) -- the day the rent increase takes effect, if the event is a rent notice` `the lessor gives notice approving a request to keep a pet under s 50B(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 7D: a Foyer Oxford fixed term of 42 days (6 weeks) takes 7 days' notice under s 70A(3); one of 43 days,
-- or a renewal, takes 30.
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`the Foyer Oxford term, in days:` k MEANS `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH `name` IS "FO", `lessor` IS "Foundation Housing Limited", `granted by` IS "Foundation Housing Limited", `tenants` IS (LIST "T1"), `premises` IS "Foyer Oxford unit 1", `kind` IS `a tenancy for a fixed term`, `rent basis` IS `a fixed amount`, `entered into on` IS `day number` 2026 2 1, `tenancy commenced on` IS `day number` 2026 2 1, `expiry day` IS JUST (`day number` 2026 2 1 PLUS k MINUS 1), `weekly rent` IS 200, `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE, `provides that the rent may increase` IS FALSE, `rent increases excluded by agreement` IS FALSE, `notices under s 70A` IS EMPTY, `possession delivered up on` IS NOTHING, `terminated on` IS NOTHING, `status` IS (`the status with only limb set:` 10)
#ASSERT `r 7D -- applies to` (`the Foyer Oxford term, in days:` 42)
#ASSERT `s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D where it applies -- the number of days` (`the Foyer Oxford term, in days:` 42) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT NOT (`r 7D -- applies to` (`the Foyer Oxford term, in days:` 43))
#ASSERT `s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D where it applies -- the number of days` (`the Foyer Oxford term, in days:` 43) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D where it applies -- the number of days` `a fixed term F for 2026` EQUALS 30
-- r 7F: s 82 does not apply to the Housing Authority's and WACHS sub-letting agreements.
#ASSERT `r 7F -- section 82 does not apply to` (`P with status` (`the status with only limb set:` 8))
#ASSERT `r 7F -- section 82 does not apply to` (`P with status` (`the status with only limb set:` 9))
#ASSERT NOT (`r 7F -- section 82 does not apply to` `a periodic agreement P`)
-- r 10AD and FK-14: $500 or less: $50; over $500: $100; south of the 26th parallel at $1 200 or more: $1 200
-- on the reading taken (A), $100 on reading B; north of it at $1 200: $100.
#ASSERT `r 10AD -- the amount prescribed for s 27(2)(a), at weekly rent` 500 `south of the 26th parallel:` TRUE EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `r 10AD -- the amount prescribed for s 27(2)(a), at weekly rent` 501 `south of the 26th parallel:` TRUE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `r 10AD -- the amount prescribed for s 27(2)(a), at weekly rent` 1199 `south of the 26th parallel:` TRUE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `r 10AD -- the amount prescribed for s 27(2)(a), at weekly rent` 1200 `south of the 26th parallel:` TRUE EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `FK-14 reading B -- r 10AD -- the amount prescribed, at weekly rent` 1200 `south of the 26th parallel:` TRUE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `r 10AD -- the amount prescribed for s 27(2)(a), at weekly rent` 1200 `south of the 26th parallel:` FALSE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `r 10AD -- row 2 describes an agreement at weekly rent` 1200 AND `r 10AD -- row 3 describes an agreement at weekly rent` 1200 `south of the 26th parallel:` TRUE
-- r 10A and r 11.
#ASSERT `r 10A -- the amount prescribed for s 29(1)(b)(ii)` EQUALS 350
#ASSERT `r 11 -- the amount prescribed for s 29(2)` EQUALS 1200

§ `Section 85 (with rr 7FA and 12I), and section 82 (with r 7F)`

GIVEN w IS A `Way of giving a notice`, k IS A `Kind of notice`, consent IS A BOOLEAN, ha IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Giving of a notice`
`a notice given` w `of kind` k `, consent:` consent `, by the Housing Authority:` ha MEANS
    `Giving of a notice` WITH
        `way`                                                      IS w
        `kind of notice`                                           IS k
        `on`                                                       IS `day number` 2026 3 2
        `day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS `day number` 2026 3 5
        `the recipient consented to electronic service`            IS consent
        `the recipient's email was given to the bond administrator with a bond record or release application` IS FALSE
        `the Housing Authority is the lessor and gives it`         IS ha

`an in-scope notice` MEANS `a notice under an in-scope provision (ss 30, 31A, 31, 64, 70A)`

#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `personally (s 85(1)(a))` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` FALSE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 3 2)
-- s 85(2): a posted notice is given when it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `by post (s 85(1)(b))` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` FALSE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 3 5)
-- FK-12: an in-scope notice emailed to a tenant who consented: not given under s 85 (A); given on the day sent (B).
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `by email (s 85(1)(c))` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` TRUE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `FK-12 reading B -- s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `by email (s 85(1)(c))` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` TRUE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 3 2)
-- r 12I: an authorised notice emailed with consent is given; without consent or prescribed circumstances it is not.
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `by email (s 85(1)(c))` `of kind` `an authorised notice (r 12I(1))` `, consent:` TRUE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `by email (s 85(1)(c))` `of kind` `an authorised notice (r 12I(1))` `, consent:` FALSE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `r 12I(2)(a) -- prescribed circumstances exist for` (`Giving of a notice` WITH `way` IS `by email (s 85(1)(c))`, `kind of notice` IS `an authorised notice (r 12I(1))`, `on` IS 0, `day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS 0, `the recipient consented to electronic service` IS FALSE, `the recipient's email was given to the bond administrator with a bond record or release application` IS TRUE, `the Housing Authority is the lessor and gives it` IS FALSE)
-- r 7FA: only the Housing Authority, as lessor, may leave a notice at the premises.
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `left at the premises by the Housing Authority (r 7FA)` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` FALSE `, by the Housing Authority:` TRUE) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `left at the premises by the Housing Authority (r 7FA)` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` FALSE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 85(4): to an apparent adult resident, or the person who ordinarily pays the rent.
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `to a person apparently over 16 apparently residing at the premises (s 85(4)(a))` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` FALSE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (`a notice given` `to the person who ordinarily pays the rent (s 85(4)(b))` `of kind` `an in-scope notice` `, consent:` FALSE `, by the Housing Authority:` FALSE) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 3 2)
-- s 85(3), (5), (6).
#ASSERT `s 85(3) -- the notice is deemed to have been given` (`Substituted giving` WITH `the notice cannot be given under s 85(1)` IS TRUE, `a copy published in a daily newspaper circulating in the State` IS TRUE, `a court-ordered alternative means effected` IS FALSE, `made publicly available in a prescribed manner` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 85(3) -- the notice is deemed to have been given` (`Substituted giving` WITH `the notice cannot be given under s 85(1)` IS FALSE, `a copy published in a daily newspaper circulating in the State` IS TRUE, `a court-ordered alternative means effected` IS FALSE, `made publicly available in a prescribed manner` IS FALSE))
