§ `Part IV -- ss 27, 27AA, 28 and 29`

GIVEN kd IS A `Kind of amount`, amt IS A NUMBER, wr IS A NUMBER, south IS A BOOLEAN, fate IS A `What became of an option fee`
GIVETH AN `Amount required or received`
`an amount of kind` kd `of` amt `at weekly rent` wr `, south:` south `, the fee's fate:` fate MEANS
    `Amount required or received` WITH `kind` IS kd, `amount` IS amt, `weekly rent under the agreement` IS wr, `the premises are south of the 26th parallel` IS south, `what became of the option fee` IS fate

`an option fee` MEANS `consideration for an option to enter into a residential tenancy agreement`
GIVEN rd IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of an option fee`
`refused 2 March, refunded on day` rd MEANS `the option was refused and the fee refunded in cash or by electronic means` (`day number` 2026 3 2) rd
GIVEN rd IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of an option fee`
`refused Sunday 1 March, refunded on day` rd MEANS `the option was refused and the fee refunded in cash or by electronic means` (`day number` 2026 3 1) rd

-- s 27(2)(a): $100 at $600 a week, refused Monday 2 March 2026 and refunded electronically on Monday 9 March,
-- within 7 days: excepted; on 10 March: not. Refused Sunday 1 March: the 7th day after is Sunday 8 March, so
-- a refund on Monday 9 March is in time (Interpretation Act s 61(1)(e)). $150: over the prescribed amount;
-- $1 000 at $1 200 a week south of the 26th parallel: within the amount prescribed on FK-14 reading A.
